// expect-exit: 0
mod:list_ptr_through_param_ok;
// WHAT DEF-584 LEAVES LEGAL (landing 177d2b3), each module one cell that reads its own right value (67 or 127), the same on every build and under the freed-heap
// detector: the calls of `list_ptr_through_param.npk` with nothing growing or replacing the `List` (`xb1c`, `xb4c`, `xr1c`, `xk1c`, `xp2c`, `xd5c`) or with the
// pointer re-pointed first (`xr5`); A VALUE READ OUT OF A PARAMETER THAT HOLDS NO ADDRESS (`xo1`, the prelude's `T:out = move(l.items[i]);` and then writes of
// `l.items`; `xo1b` a member; `xo1c` an index); a copy of the parameter, which is no pointer into it (`xo4`); a pointee that holds no `List` (`xm11`, `xq6`, and
// `xo5` an enum holder over one); the element read before the growth and not after (`xq7`), another pointee grown (`xq8`), a value member (`xq9`), a store read
// back through the parameter (`xp1l`); a pointer TO the struct as a temporary (`xk7`; a `dyn` temporary over a pointee with no `List`, `xk5`, is in `list_ptr_from_call_dyn_ok.npk`, DEF-463); THE PARAMETER'S OWN
// REASSIGNMENT, which leaves its old pointee alone (`xr6`, `xr7`, and `xr8` in a later argument's arm while the temporary is live); an enum pointee's price not paid
// in the parameter form (`xg3`; its local twin is DEF-575's price); A `wild` SLOT'S VALUE, WHICH ASKS NOTHING (`xw1`, the wild vector's `#wild_slice` idiom: manual
// storage is the author's to keep); and the `any->` price's two neighbours, its local twin (`xpr1l`) and the same casts with nothing written (`xpr1c`).
error:Bad;
